  "id": "testamentary-capacity",
  "term": "testamentary capacity",
  "definition": "Testamentary capacity is the legal ability to make a will, judged in relation to that specific act. A person may still have this capacity despite mental unsoundness in other respects, unless a delusion or disturbance bears directly on what is involved in the will.",
